## Day 2

### Peripheral Devices
- *Sequencing note: build this before going deep on Spectral Signals below. Not a hard technical dependency for SpectralDrawer/SpectralFilter (those work fine on any buffer, e.g. a loaded file), but real vocal/mic material is the actual motivating use case for the spectral work, and audio input exercises realtime plumbing (device callback timing, block size, clock) that's better shaken out on its own before also debugging STFT hop-rate scheduling on top of it.*
- [Big] Support Audio Input peripherals. Eagerly convert input to the audio output device's rate/blocksize (already treated as ground truth throughout the graph) at ingestion, so the rest of the graph only ever sees one uniform clock domain. Conversion (resample + re-block + jitter buffer) happens inside the peripheral component's implementation — no user-facing seam; component just presents a single `AudioSignal` output. Device selection / input gain are fine to expose; resampling internals are not.
- [Big] Allow multiple MIDI peripheral devices
- [Big] Support MIDI output peripherals

### Spectral / Frequency-Domain Components
- *Dependency: none of the existing component classes (Audio Signal / Audio Buffer) natively carry frequency-domain data. This needs a new data type before any spectral component can be built*
- [Big] Define `SpectralBuffer` type (array of frames, each frame an array of complex bins, plus metadata: FFT size, hop size, window type, sample rate) for offline/non-causal use — full buffer available up front, all frames materialized and randomly accessible.
- [Big] Define `SpectralStream` type — same per-frame content as `SpectralBuffer`, but emitted one frame per hop in realtime. Runs at hop-rate, not sample-rate, so the graph's scheduling/clock model needs to account for a non-audio-rate signal type.
- [Medium] `Buffer -> SpectralBuffer` Translation Component (offline STFT)
- [Medium] `SpectralBuffer -> Buffer` Translation Component (offline ISTFT)
- [Medium] `AudioSignal -> SpectralStream` Translation Component (realtime STFT)
- [Medium] `SpectralStream -> AudioSignal` Translation Component (realtime ISTFT)
- Both STFT/ISTFT pairs should share one underlying engine (same window/hop/FFT math) — offline mode just runs it across all frames at once, realtime mode runs it one hop at a time.

### New Components
- [Quick] `Bitcrusher` -- reduce audio resolution ( audio in, audio out)
- [Quick] `AudioSwitch` -- switch audio through output channel 0 or 1 (audio in, 2 audio out)
- [Quick] `MidiSwitch` -- leverage midi channel system? (midi in, midi out) 
- [Quick] `Quantizer` -- real time midi manipulation and routing (midi in, midi out)
- [Quick] `MidiOffset` -- set offsets note values, velocity values (midi in, midi out)
- [Medium] `PitchShifter` -- maybe buffer + real time versions? *Note: a PSOLA-based version (pitch-mark detection + grain windowing + overlap-add) may be buildable on top of existing/planned grain-OLA primitives without depending on the SpectralBuffer/SpectralStream work below — worth scoping separately from the spectral-domain pitch shifting.*
- [Big] `SpectralDrawer` -- Allow a user to build a spectrograph (buffer out). *Depends on `SpectralBuffer` type + `Buffer -> SpectralBuffer` translation.*
- [Big] `SpectralFilter` -- Spectrogram of input buffer, with option to filter out frequency bands (buffer in, buffer out). *Depends on `SpectralBuffer` type + STFT/ISTFT translation components. Magnitude-only edits (boost/cut bins, keep original phase) are safe/low-risk; anything that moves content in frequency or time will need phase-locking handling later.*
- [Big] `Mixer` *note: investigate whether this should be a primary component or a configured GroupComponent (e.g., chained panners with some scalar controls or something)*

